IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `crm-time`
IMPORT `crm-penalties`
IMPORT `crm-offences`
IMPORT `crm-liability`
IMPORT `crm-seat`

-- Worked cases for crm-seat.l4: at least one for each question, with the facts a
-- person in the seat would state, the boundary on each side of every threshold,
-- and a case the text does not answer. Every expected value is written from the
-- text of ss 3, 4A to 4N before the case was run; none is copied from output.

§ `Cases for the seat: working out the most that can be imposed`


§§ `What a penalty unit comes to in dollars (s 4AA)`

-- Before the first indexation day (1 July 2026) a penalty unit is $330.
#ASSERT `What is a penalty unit worth` (Date 30 6 2026) 330 0 0 EQUALS JUST 330
#ASSERT `What is a penalty unit worth` (Date 1 1 2020) 330 0 0 EQUALS JUST 330
-- On 1 July 2026 the amount is replaced: 330 x (130 / 125 = 1.04) = 343.2, to the nearest dollar 343. It applies to an offence on that day and after.
#ASSERT `What is a penalty unit worth` (Date 1 7 2026) 330 130 125 EQUALS JUST 343
#ASSERT `What is a penalty unit worth` (Date 31 12 2028) 330 130 125 EQUALS JUST 343
-- The next indexation day is 1 July 2029: 343 x (135 / 130 = 1.03846, to 3 places 1.038) = 356.034, so 356.
#ASSERT `What is a penalty unit worth` (Date 30 6 2029) 330 130 125 EQUALS JUST 343
#ASSERT `What is a penalty unit worth` (Date 1 7 2029) 343 135 130 EQUALS JUST 356
-- Without a base quarter index number the factor cannot be worked out.
#ASSERT `What is a penalty unit worth` (Date 1 7 2026) 330 130 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `What does a penalty of so many penalty units come to in dollars` 5 (Date 1 7 2026) 330 130 125 EQUALS JUST 1715
#ASSERT `What does a penalty of so many penalty units come to in dollars` 60 (Date 30 6 2026) 330 0 0 EQUALS JUST 19800
#ASSERT `What does a penalty of so many penalty units come to in dollars` 0 (Date 30 6 2026) 330 0 0 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `What does a penalty of so many penalty units come to in dollars` 10 (Date 1 7 2026) 330 130 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `A penalty stated in dollars (s 4AB)`

-- The arguments: the dollar amount; in a law of the Commonwealth or a Territory Ordinance; the maximum amount of a penalty; imposed by a court or service tribunal; section 76 of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010; a prescribed provision.
#ASSERT `How many penalty units is a penalty stated in dollars taken to be` 250 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS (`converted to penalty units` 3)
#ASSERT `How many penalty units is a penalty stated in dollars taken to be` 200 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS (`converted to penalty units` 2)
#ASSERT `How many penalty units is a penalty stated in dollars taken to be` 100 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS (`converted to penalty units` 1)
#ASSERT `How many penalty units is a penalty stated in dollars taken to be` 101 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS (`converted to penalty units` 2)
#ASSERT `How many penalty units is a penalty stated in dollars taken to be` 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS (`converted to penalty units` 0)
#ASSERT `How many penalty units is a penalty stated in dollars taken to be` 250 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS (`converted to penalty units` 3)
#ASSERT `How many penalty units is a penalty stated in dollars taken to be` 250 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the text says the conversion does not apply`
#ASSERT `How many penalty units is a penalty stated in dollars taken to be` 250 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the text says the conversion does not apply`
#ASSERT `How many penalty units is a penalty stated in dollars taken to be` 250 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the text says the conversion does not apply`
#ASSERT `How many penalty units is a penalty stated in dollars taken to be` 250 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the text does not say how this converts`

§§ `What a court may fine a natural person or a body corporate (s 4B)`

-- The arguments: a natural person convicted; imprisonment only; imprisonment for life; the longest term in months; a contrary intention appears; the court thinks it appropriate.
#ASSERT `What is the most pecuniary penalty a court may impose on a natural person` TRUE TRUE FALSE 12 FALSE TRUE EQUALS (`no more than this` 60)
#ASSERT `What is the most pecuniary penalty a court may impose on a natural person` TRUE TRUE FALSE 24 FALSE TRUE EQUALS (`no more than this` 120)
#ASSERT `What is the most pecuniary penalty a court may impose on a natural person` TRUE TRUE FALSE 6 FALSE TRUE EQUALS (`no more than this` 30)
#ASSERT `What is the most pecuniary penalty a court may impose on a natural person` TRUE TRUE FALSE 120 FALSE TRUE EQUALS (`no more than this` 600)
#ASSERT `What is the most pecuniary penalty a court may impose on a natural person` TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 FALSE TRUE EQUALS (`no more than this` 2000)
#ASSERT `What is the most pecuniary penalty a court may impose on a natural person` TRUE TRUE FALSE 12 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `none is allowed by this provision`
#ASSERT `What is the most pecuniary penalty a court may impose on a natural person` TRUE TRUE FALSE 12 TRUE TRUE EQUALS `none is allowed by this provision`
#ASSERT `What is the most pecuniary penalty a court may impose on a natural person` FALSE TRUE FALSE 12 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `none is allowed by this provision`
#ASSERT `What is the most pecuniary penalty a court may impose on a natural person` TRUE FALSE FALSE 12 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `none is allowed by this provision`
#ASSERT `What is the most pecuniary penalty a court may impose on a natural person` TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 TRUE TRUE EQUALS `none is allowed by this provision`
#ASSERT `What is the most pecuniary penalty a court may impose on a natural person` TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `none is allowed by this provision`
-- A term of no months is not a term the formula can use.
#ASSERT `What is the most pecuniary penalty a court may impose on a natural person` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the text does not say`
-- The arguments: a body corporate convicted; a contrary intention appears; the court thinks fit; the most a natural person could be fined for the same offence.
#ASSERT `What is the most pecuniary penalty a court may impose on a body corporate` TRUE FALSE TRUE 60 EQUALS (`no more than this` 300)
#ASSERT `What is the most pecuniary penalty a court may impose on a body corporate` TRUE FALSE TRUE 2000 EQUALS (`no more than this` 10000)
#ASSERT `What is the most pecuniary penalty a court may impose on a body corporate` TRUE FALSE TRUE 0 EQUALS (`no more than this` 0)
#ASSERT `What is the most pecuniary penalty a court may impose on a body corporate` TRUE TRUE TRUE 60 EQUALS `none is allowed by this provision`
#ASSERT `What is the most pecuniary penalty a court may impose on a body corporate` TRUE FALSE FALSE 60 EQUALS `none is allowed by this provision`
#ASSERT `What is the most pecuniary penalty a court may impose on a body corporate` FALSE FALSE TRUE 60 EQUALS `none is allowed by this provision`

